<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simon de Montfort, 6th Earl of Leicester</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1208–1265</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simon de Montfort, 6th Earl of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leicester">Leicester</a>, was a French-born noble, a son of the leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>, who became leader of the baronial opposition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a>. He defeated the king at Lewes in 1264 and governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, summoning in 1265 a parliament that included knights of the shires and burgesses of the towns. He was killed at the Battle of Evesham in 1265.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simon-de-montfort-6th-earl-of-leicester.jpg" alt="Simon de Montfort, 6th Earl of Leicester" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simon_Leicester.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
